# Rover P5B 3.5 Litre four-door coupe, 1967-1973.
#
# The V8 P5 coupe: the ex-Buick 3.5-litre engine in the four-door coupe body,
# with the lowered roofline, thinner B-pillars, V8 grille and badges. 9,099
# coupes were built. The fastest and most sought-after P5.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P5
#
# Dimensions 4.724 x 1.778 x 1.397 m, wheelbase 2.794 m (coupe roof height).
#
# Shape reference: the coupe uses the P5 three-quarter photographs and the
# P5B saloon's front and rear detail; there is no dedicated coupe side
# elevation in the pack. The flank and the lower roofline are estimated from
# the coupe photographs and the published dimensions; the limitation is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: documented Rover finishes of the period: Arden Green, Sierra
# Beige, Mexico Brown, Black. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 180 km/h. Comfort 120/510, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 120, the same
# spacious cabin as the P5B saloon. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1967 intro, retires staggered 1986-1989.
#
# The four-door coupe's roof is lower than the saloon's: 1.397 m is the
# model's height. 9,099 P5B coupes were built.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-p5b-coupe.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-p5b-coupe.dae. References:
# citycars/references/rover-p5b-coupe/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the body and lowered roof come from the P5 coupe master
# and the V8 grille, badges and rear trim from the P5B saloon photographs; there
# is no dedicated P5B coupe side elevation. The grille treatment is simplified
# and the rear V8 trim is not photograph-verified. At 128 px the lowered roof,
# V8 grille and badges read as a P5B coupe.


obj=citycar
name=RoverP5BCoupe(ArdenGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1967
intro_month=9
retire_year=1989
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=120
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=510

